  "notes": [
   "The certificate section lists no courses itself; it says the 40 units of Required Courses and 8 units of Electives are those listed under the A.A. degree in Electrical Construction and Maintenance: Construction Technician, so the blocks are read from that A.A. section.",
   "The semester 'ELECTIVE' rows (2+3+3 = 8 units) are the Major Electives block's 8 units and are not recorded separately as open electives.",
   "The Major Electives block prints only 'Select at least 8 units'; no separate block total is printed, so stated is null.",
   "The PLOs are printed once for the Electrical Construction and Maintenance programs as a whole ('Upon completion of the Degree/Certificate programs'); this certificate shares that list.",
   "Careers are taken from the shared program overview, which applies to all Electrical Construction and Maintenance awards.",
   "ECONMT 001, 006 and 007 are printed with leading zeros; they were matched to closed-list ECONMT 1, 6 and 7. ECONMT 215 was matched to closed-list 'ECONMT215', which has no space.",
   "ECONMT 129 appears both as a required course (Semester II) and in the Major Electives list; it is recorded in both blocks as printed.",
   "The catalog prints ECONMT 164 at 3 units and titles it 'Sustainable Lighting'; the closed list stores it at 4 units."
